    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query molecule.",
    "No IV/oral AUC comparison is available for lenalidomide or an exact structural analog.",
    "No query-specific hepatic clearance or metabolic-stability assay is available; thalidomide and lactam-analog data are indirect.",
    "No query-specific Caco-2/PAMPA permeability or P-gp/BCRP efflux assay is available; C213 is a larger lenalidomide-warhead degrader.",
    "No fed/fasted or formulation-specific bioavailability data for the query.",
    "No human in vivo clearance data for the query's primary aromatic amine/imide metabolic routes."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F >= 20%) is retained and modestly strengthened. L6 adds indirect but supportive hepatic-clearance evidence: thalidomide shows low human in vitro metabolic clearance and minimal CYP involvement (C260, C229), and a lactam analog is metabolically stable in human liver microsomes and rat hepatocytes (C218). C259, a high-clearance large PROTAC containing a lenalidomide warhead, has low transferability and does not contradict the prediction. No direct F measurement exists, so confidence remains moderate."
}

